-- lib/lang/rust/read.cub — the reading of MIR, third part: statements, terminators, frames,
-- the table of a crate's instances, the run by fuel, static storage, and the entry.
--
--
--   rust-init t crate          a program's static storage made: its statics, then its vtables;
--                              the value is the image, their addresses as slots
--   rust-call t crate fuel image j args    instance j (an index into the crate's instances) applied
--   rust-entry t crate fuel image args     the crate's entry body
-- An argument and a result are slots: sl-reg of a value for a register class; for an object,
-- sl-mem of an allocation holding it, made by the caller, owned (and released) by the callee
-- when an argument and by the caller when a result.
--
-- Fuel. One %welimP on the fuel runs everything: each block entered spends one, in the body
-- running and in every body that called it (a call runs the callee with the fuel left at the
-- calling block). Spent, the meaning is mstop st-fuel.
import "read-rvalue.hypercubical"

